        tabLabel: 'About',
        pages: [
          {
            title: 'Tute americano',
            subtitle: 'Card Game',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Tute americano: Tute variant with American deck (52 cards) or 40-card strip. Same point-trick and Cantes logic; variant rules.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Tute originated in Italy as tutti and spread to Spain in the 19th century, becoming one of the most popular card games there and in Latin America. Tute americano is a two-player variant that follows the same point-trick and marriage (cantes) logic as Tute corriente but is played with a 40- or 52-card deck and differs in hand size (eight cards), no tute declaration, and a 121-point target.',
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Two players only; no partnerships. Non-dealer leads first; turn to deal alternates.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '40-card pack (Spanish or French stripped).',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Cards',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Eight cards each, one at a time; turn one face up for trump; rest form stock.',
              },
            ],
          },
        ],
      },
